commit ca7735ec806eaed474fe9303ab85010ab3b226e2
Author: Prasad Shirvalkar <prasad.shirvalkar@ucsf.edu>
Date:   Sat Jun 27 02:25:11 2026 -0700

    CS-2: event-PSD taxonomy — surface Streaming as its own category, fix Montage PSD mislabel
    
    Three PSD-bearing event sources were conflated. Define PSD_SOURCE_TAXONOMY as
    the single source of truth and route each consistently across loader, timeline
    assembler, and frontend legend.
    
    - Un-exclude Streaming: remove _EVENT_NAME_EXCLUDE; _load_patient_events now
      surfaces all 2700 PatientControllerEvent PSDs (2479 Streaming + 221 labeled),
      each tagged category via _event_display_category (Streaming vs labeled share
      the EVENT_PSD_SOURCE pooling tag but get distinct display categories).
    - event_markers threads category through + returns categories[].
    - _load_montage_psd_events tags NeuralActivitySnapshot markers
      DISPLAY_MONTAGE_SNAPSHOT (a montage product carrying its OWN TD, distinct from
      PSD-only patient events).
    - Frontend: EVENTS diamond row shows only labeled presses (Streaming render as
      per-lane teal event-PSD ticks, not flooding the row); count label 'N labeled
      · M streaming'; legend split into grey montage vs teal streaming/event PSD,
      added the missing patient-event diamond glyph, fixed stale 'survey PSD x 269'
      -> 'transform DSP -> LSB'.
    - Encodes the LSB routing rule (TD present -> td_transform k=352.62; PSD-only
      patient events -> psd_bridge) that CS-3 consumes.
    
    Tests: +7 (taxonomy invariants, display-category split, category threading).
    Suite 210/210.

